    "rationale": "All 60 evaluations so far are unrolled_k and 0/60 feasible. The binding constraints are throughput_msps >= 32 and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44: best unrolled_k throughput is only 9.97 MSPS and best sys_p99_batch is 3.2 us, both structurally limited by multi-cycle shared-FSM scheduling. Accuracy is not the bottleneck: best max_abs_err seen is 2^-16.11, far below the required 2^-12. iterative is even worse for throughput, so the missing families that can produce one result per cycle are pipelined and pipelined_m. Explore those next, with n_iter biased low for latency and data_width/guards wide enough to keep accuracy above 12 bits."
  }
, "rationale": "0/60 feasible; all unrolled_k violate throughput (best 9.97 < 32) and sys_p99_batch (best 3.2 > 0.44). Accuracy already exceeds the spec (best 2^-16.11 vs 2^-12), so the bottleneck is results/cycle and burst latency. Only pipelined / pipelined_m offer 1 result/cycle; iterative and unrolled_k with shared FSM cannot plausibly close the 3.2 us -> 0.44 us gap. Add those families next."

